            <ArticleTitle>Approaches to senior care #6. Shoulder pain in the geriatric patient. Part I. Evaluation and pathophysiology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>129-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Shoulder pain is one of the most common musculoskeletal complaints in the elderly. The rewards of accurate diagnosis and early treatment often elude the orthopaedist without a systematic approach to this region. A thorough understanding of shoulder anatomy, pain referral patterns, and the pathophysiology of the aging process must be combined with an awareness of the latest treatment modalities and surgical techniques.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
